        "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <iterator>\n#include <limits>\n#include <string>\n#include <vector>\n\nnamespace {\n\nstatic bool is_whitespace(char c)\n{\n    return c == ' ' || c == '\\n' || c == '\\r' || c == '\\t'\n        || c == '\\f' || c == '\\v';\n}\n\nstatic std::string read_text()\n{\n    std::istreambuf_iterator<char> first(std::cin);\n    std::istreambuf_iterator<char> last;\n    std::string text(first, last);\n    text.erase(std::remove_if(text.begin(), text.end(), is_whitespace), text.end());\n    return text;\n}\n\nstatic void write_line(const std::string& text)\n{\n    std::cout.put('[');\n    std::cout.put(' ');\n    for (std::string::const_iterator it = text.begin(); it != text.end(); ++it) {\n        std::cout.put(*it);\n        std::cout.put(' ');\n    }\n    std::cout.put(']');\n    std::cout.put('\\n');\n}\n\nstatic inline void format_line(const char* source, std::size_t length, char* destination)\n{\n    *destination++ = '[';\n    *destination++ = ' ';\n    for (std::size_t index = 0; index != length; ++index) {\n        *destination++ = source[index];\n        *destination++ = ' ';\n    }\n    *destination++ = ']';\n    *destination = '\\n';\n}\n\nstatic void write_serially(std::string& text)\n{\n    do {\n        write_line(text);\n    } while (std::next_permutation(text.begin(), text.end()));\n}\n\n} // namespace\n\nint main()\n{\n    std::ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(0);\n\n    std::string text = read_text();\n    if (text.empty()) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    std::sort(text.begin(), text.end());\n\n    const std::size_t length = text.size();\n    const std::size_t limit = std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max();\n    if (length > (limit - 4u) / 2u) {\n        write_serially(text);\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const std::size_t line_bytes = length * 2u + 4u;\n    if (length > limit - line_bytes) {\n        write_serially(text);\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const std::size_t item_bytes = length + line_bytes;\n    const std::size_t batch_budget = 4u * 1024u * 1024u;\n    if (item_bytes > batch_budget) {\n        write_serially(text);\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const std::size_t capacity = batch_budget / item_bytes;\n    std::vector<char> rows(capacity * length);\n    std::vector<char> output(capacity * line_bytes);\n    bool has_more = true;\n\n    while (has_more) {\n        std::size_t count = 0;\n        do {\n            std::copy(text.begin(), text.end(), rows.begin() + count * length);\n            ++count;\n            has_more = std::next_permutation(text.begin(), text.end());\n        } while (has_more && count != capacity);\n\n        if (count < 256u) {\n            for (std::size_t record = 0; record != count; ++record) {\n                format_line(&rows[record * length], length, &output[record * line_bytes]);\n            }\n        } else {\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n            for (std::size_t record = 0; record < count; ++record) {\n                format_line(&rows[record * length], length, &output[record * line_bytes]);\n            }\n        }\n\n        std::cout.write(&output[0], static_cast<std::streamsize>(count * line_bytes));\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/permutations.cc"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Batching lexicographically generated permutations into bounded fixed-width rows enables race-free static OpenMP serialization, while one ordered bulk write per batch removes per-line stream synchronization and flushing overhead.",
    "notes": "Uses at most a 4 MiB staging/output batch and falls back to streaming serialization when a single record exceeds that bound.",
